{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Life cycles: mammal, amphibian, insect and bird","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#1d3557","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"Which animal goes through a larva stage and a pupa stage before it becomes an adult?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"A butterfly","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"A cat","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"A frog","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Metamorphosis"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-x","content":"A big change in body shape as an animal grows up, such as a caterpillar becoming a butterfly."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which animal is born alive and feeds its young on milk?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A rabbit","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A frogspawn tadpole","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A hen's egg","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"You find a pond with frogspawn and a bird's nest. Which do you watch first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"The frogspawn","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"The bird's nest","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Over the weeks, the eggs hatch into tadpoles that grow legs and become frogs. You have watched a life cycle with a water stage."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"The eggs in the nest hatch, and the chicks are fed by their parents until they can fly. You have watched a bird's life cycle begin."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Which animal's young look like small adults from the day they hatch?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"A bird","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"A cow","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"A beetle","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"How many stages does a frog's life cycle have?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Two","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Four","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Six","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Lifecycle"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-x","content":"The stages an living thing passes through from birth to adult, and then to making new young of its own."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which animal's young are called nymphs as they grow, with no pupa stage?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"A grasshopper","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"A butterfly","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"A toad","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-t","content":"You finished the life cycles lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. You can now describe how a mammal, an amphibian, an insect and a bird grow and change."}],"actions":[]}}
